---
import Button from "./Button.astro";
---

<div class="workspace-quickstart-card">
  <div class="workspace-quickstart-header">
    <strong>How a connected Syntila Workspace powers a Space:</strong> every AI Worker executes locally through the headless <code>syntila</code> service and CLI Worker Engine on a machine controlled by a Space member.
  </div>
  <ol class="workspace-quickstart-steps" role="list">
    <li class="workspace-quickstart-step">
      <span class="workspace-step-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <div><strong>Install Workspace</strong><p>Install the Syntila Workspace service and <code>syntila</code> CLI on macOS, Windows, or Linux.</p></div>
    </li>
    <li class="workspace-quickstart-step">
      <span class="workspace-step-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <div><strong>Run <code>syntila setup</code></strong><p>Link your machine to your Syntila account and detect installed provider CLIs.</p></div>
    </li>
    <li class="workspace-quickstart-step">
      <span class="workspace-step-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <div><strong>Grant to a Space</strong><p>Choose which Spaces can use your Workspace and which AI Workers are enabled.</p></div>
    </li>
    <li class="workspace-quickstart-step">
      <span class="workspace-step-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
      <div><strong>Collaborate in Syntila</strong><p>Everyone in the Space can now prompt those Workers in shared Threads at <code>syntila.app</code> on web, iOS, and Android.</p></div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="workspace-quickstart-cta">
    <Button href="/downloads/" label="Download Syntila Workspace →" variant="secondary" />
    <Button href="https://syntila.app" label="Open Syntila" event="cta.open_app" />
  </div>
</div>
